    "q-61650": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61650",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Rose's initial salary was $$10\\,000$, and her salary increased by $12%$ per year. To the nearest $$10$, what was Rose's salary $3$ years later?",
      "worked_solution": "Rose received $$10\\,000$ initially, and this amount increased by $12%$ each year.\n\n$12%$ as a decimal is $0.12.$ Therefore, an increase of $12%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of\n\n$$\n1+0.12=1.12.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- After $1$ year, Rose received $10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, Rose received $10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, Rose received $10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)^{3}$ dollars.\n\nEvaluating the expression for the amount of money received after $3$ years, we get\n\n$$\n10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)^{3}≈14\\,050.\n$$\n\nAfter $3$ years, Rose received approximately $14\\,050$ dollars.",
